# =============================================================================
# This repository is published out of a ~20 GB working tree that contains a
# live bot token, two bot configs, dozens of 13 MB nets, three virtualenvs and
# 6 GB of built tablebase. A deny-list is one forgotten pattern away from
# publishing a credential, and the forgotten pattern is never the one you
# thought of.
#
# So this file DENIES EVERYTHING FIRST (section 1) and then names what ships
# (section 2). Section 3 is a second, independent gate: in gitignore the LAST
# matching rule wins, so nothing in section 2 can re-include a secret.
#
# general/publish_check.py enforces the same policy by a separate code path
# and prints the manifest. Run it before every push:
#
#     python3 general/publish_check.py
#
# If you add a directory to the project, it ships NOTHING until you add it to
# section 2 here AND to ALLOW in publish_check.py. That is deliberate.
# =============================================================================

# --- 1. deny everything, but keep descending into directories ---------------
*
!*/

# --- 2. what ships ----------------------------------------------------------
!/.gitignore
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/RELEASE.md

# the two Stockfish ports: source and their licences
!/sf19_ports/README.md
!/sf19_ports/sf19nn/src/**
!/sf19_ports/sf19nn/build.sh
!/sf19_ports/sf19nn/Copying.txt
!/sf19_ports/sf19nn/LICENSE-sploppy-MIT
!/sf19_ports/sf19nn/NOTICE-modifications.txt
!/sf19_ports/sf19rps/src/**
!/sf19_ports/sf19rps/Copying.txt
!/sf19_ports/sf19rps/NOTICE-modifications.txt

# harness, probes and the live seat (scripts only -- no nets, no logs)
!/sf19_ports/tools/**/*.py
!/sf19_ports/tools/**/*.md
!/sf19_ports/tools/**/*.sh
!/sf19_ports/live/**/*.py
!/sf19_ports/live/**/*.md
!/sf19_ports/live/LICENSE-sploppy-MIT

# the tablebase: solver, prober and oracle. The BUILT tables never ship
# (2.865 GiB); section 3 blocks them and RELEASE.md gives the build recipe.
!/tablebase/**/*.py
!/tablebase/**/*.c
!/tablebase/**/*.md

# the trainer: code and notes, never datasets or checkpoints
!/nnue_train/**/*.py
!/nnue_train/**/*.md

# cloud costing, the burn monitor, the publish gate, the idea ledger
!/general/**/*.py
!/general/**/*.md
!/general/**/*.json

# --- 3. hard denies. Last rule wins, so these beat every line above. --------

# credentials. Non-negotiable.
connect_bot.py
connect_bot2.py
rpsbot.conf
rpsbot2.conf
*.conf
.env
.env.*
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*.pem
*.key

# trees that hold the above, or are off limits by standing instruction
/project_files/
/RandomShitIWillNeverUseAgain/
sep2026/

# a vendored git checkout -- ship a submodule or a pointer, not a copy
**/sploppy_repo/

# environments and build detritus
**/__pycache__/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/site-packages/
**/.idea/
**/.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.orig
*.rej

# weights, data, built tables and logs. Big, regenerable, or both.
*.nnue
*.dtz
*.dtz.zst
*.tbz
*.zst
*.pt
*.pth
*.npy
*.npz
*.bin
*.log
*.journal
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip

# the built tablebase, in both formats, and the scratch dir the scripts write into.
# NOTE: tablebase/tb5_build/ is NOT built output -- it is 1.4 MB of solver source
# and small audit artifacts, so it is not denied here. The built tables are
# tb5_zst/ (.dtz.zst) and probe/tbz/ (.tbz).
/tablebase/tb5_zst/
/tablebase/probe/tbz/
/tablebase/probe/tb_pack
/work/
**/work/

# compiled engines: GPL source ships, binaries do not
/sf19_ports/sf19nn/stockfish
/sf19_ports/sf19rps/stockfish
/sf19_ports/live/stockfish
